<a name="TIMELINE">

<ol> 
<li> May 1991 - Became bedsheet format. Decreased number of pages from 164
		to 96. Kim Mohan took over as editor. Increased the
		price from $1.75 to $3.95. Began publishing monthly.
<li> Sep 1986 - Patrick Lucien Price took over as editor.
<li> Jan 1984 - Increased the price from $1.50 to $1.75.
<li> Mar 1982 - TSR Hobbies took over as publisher. George H. Scithers
		took over as editor.
<li> ??? 198? - Title became <i>Amazing Science Fiction Stories</i>.
<li> Nov 1980 - Combined with <i>Fantastic</i>.
<li> Mar 1979 - Elinor Mavor took over as editor. She used the
		pseudonym "Omar Gohagen" until Sep 1982, when she
		began using her real name.
<li> Oct 1978 - Sol Cohen sold his interest to partner Arthur Bernhard.
<li> May 1969 - Ted White took over as editor.
<li> Dec 1968 - Barry N. Malzberg took over as editor.
<li> Dec 1967 - Harry Harrison took over as editor.
<li> Aug 1965 - Sol Cohen took over as publisher (Ultimate Publishing Company).
                Joseph Ross took over as editor.
		Increased number of pages from 132 to 164.
<li> Jun 1965 - Began publishing bimonthly.
<li> May 1963 - Increased the price from $0.35 to $0.50.
<li> Sep 1962 - Decreased number of pages from 148 to 132.
<li> Oct 1960 - Title became <i>Amazing Stories</i> (Subtitled
     "Fact and Science Fiction" until Jun 1965).
<li> Dec 1958 - Cele Goldsmith took over as editor. She later married,
                changing her name to Cele Lalli for the August 1964 issue.
<li> May 1958 - Title became <i>Amazing Science Fiction Stories</i>.
<li> Mar 1958 - Title became <i>Amazing Science Fiction</i>.
<li> Nov 1955 - Began publishing monthly.
<li> Sep 1955 - Paul W. Fairman took over as editor.
<li> Apr/May 1953 - Became digest size. Began publishing bimonthly.
<li> Oct 1950 - Decreased number of pages from 180 to 164.
<li> Sep 1950 - Decreased number of pages from 196 to 180.
<li> Mar 1950 - Increased number of pages from 164 to 196.
<li> Jan 1950 - Howard Browne took over as editor.
<li> Sep 1949 - Increased number of pages from 148 to 164.
<li> Jun 1949 - Decreased number of pages from 156 to 148.
<li> Sep 1948 - Decreased number of pages from 164 to 156.
<li> Aug 1948 - Decreased number of pages from 166 to 164.
<li> Jul 1948 - Decreased number of pages from 180 to 166.
<li> May 1946 - Began publishing monthly.
<li> Sep 1945 - Decreased number of pages from 212 to 180.
<li> Sep 1943 - Began publishing bimonthly.
<li> Jun 1943 - Decreased number of pages from 244 to 212.
<li> Aug 1942 - Increased number of pages from 144 to 244.
<li> Oct 1938 - Began publishing monthly.
<li> Jun 1938 - Ziff-Davis Publishing Co. took over as publisher.
                Raymond A. Palmer took over as editor.
<li> Aug 1935 - Began publishing bimonthly.
<li> Oct 1933 - Became pulp size; increased the number of pages
		from 96 to 144.
<li> Nov 1929 - T. O'Conor Sloane took over as editor.
<li> May 1929 - Teck Pub. Corp. took over as publisher.
                Arthur Lynch took over as editor.
<li> Apr 1926 - First issue of <i>Amazing Stories</i>; bedsheet size.
     Published by Experimenter Pub. Co. Edited by Hugo Gernsback.
</ol>

